# ~/.config/DankMaterialShell is a symlink pointing HERE, so everything DMS
# writes lands in this directory. DMS owns the contents; git tracks one file.
#
# Allowlist, not denylist, on purpose: DMS creates files on demand as you use
# features -- plugin_settings.json (can hold plugin API keys), monitors.json
# (per-machine output make/model/serial), themes/<id>/theme.json (vendored
# registry themes). A denylist would silently start tracking each new one.
*
!.gitignore
!settings.json
# Display profiles: which outputs, at what scale and position, and how to match
# them. DMS regenerates niri/dms/outputs.kdl from whichever profile matches, so
# this is the source of that geometry and worth tracking. It does carry output
# make/model/serial, which is per-machine but not sensitive.
!monitors.json

# Our own plugin is source, not vendored: track it while keeping the installed
# third-party clones (each its own git repo) ignored.
!plugins/
plugins/*
!plugins/profileSwitcher/
!plugins/profileSwitcher/**

# For the record, since they are not tracked:
#   plugins/    third-party plugins, each its own git clone -- currently
#               materialWeather and dankDesktopWeather from
#               https://github.com/AvengeMedia/dms-plugins. Our own
#               profileSwitcher is exempted above and IS tracked.
#   zen.css     matugen output, regenerated on every theme change
#   .firstlaunch, .changelog-*   DMS state markers
